    "hero.badge": "In development · Pre-Alpha",
    "hero.tag": "One shared continuous universe. Everything — ships, stations, cities and the economy — is built by the players themselves.",
    "hero.tag2": "An MMO sandbox in the spirit of Dual Universe: voxels, single shard, scripting and territorial warfare.",
    "hero.cta1": "View development plan",
    "hero.cta2": "Space in pictures",

    "about.title": "What is Open Universe",
    "about.lead": "A game about freedom in a boundless universe: from mining ore in an asteroid belt to building orbital megacities and fighting for territory.",
    "about.c1t": "Single shard",
    "about.c1p": "One continuous world for every player. No clone servers — just one living universe.",
    "about.c2t": "Voxel without limits",
    "about.c2p": "Build anything from voxels: from a hand drill to entire cities and battle fleets.",
    "about.c3t": "Player economy",
    "about.c3p": "Resources, production and the market are shaped by players. Prices are born in the order book.",
    "about.c4t": "Programmable",
    "about.c4p": "Built-in scripting for autopilots, turrets and logistics. Your constructions are your code.",
    "about.c5t": "Territory and war",
    "about.c5p": "Capture and hold zones, fight orbital and planetary battles.",
    "about.c6t": "Persistence",
    "about.c6p": "The world runs 24/7. Everything built is saved — your story stays in space.",

    "gallery.title": "Space",
    "gallery.lead": "Concept art for the project: nebulae, black holes, asteroid belts and habitable planets.",
    "gallery.f1": "Carina Nebula (JWST)",
    "gallery.f2": "Black hole and jet",
    "gallery.f3": "Asteroid Gaspra (NASA)",
    "gallery.f4": "Habitable planet (Blue Marble)",
    "gallery.src": "Image credits: NASA / JPL-Caltech / STScI / ESA — public domain material.",

    "tech.title": "Technology and engine choice",
    "tech.lead": "The project's key architecture decision (ADR-0001): a <b>client on Unreal Engine 5 (C++)</b> and a <b>single shard on a custom Rust server</b>. For an MMO the engine is mostly client rendering and tools; server simulation is hand-written anyway.",
    "tech.c1t": "Client — Unreal Engine 5",
    "tech.c1p": "C++, source access, graphics, World Partition and Iris. Voxel, planets and floating origin are a custom module.",
    "tech.c2t": "Server — Rust",
    "tech.c2p": "Authoritative single-shard simulation, predictable performance and async networking. Not locked inside the engine.",
    "tech.c3t": "Protocol",
    "tech.c3p": "UDP + binary deltas with FlatBuffers/protobuf schemas — one contract shared by client and server.",
    "tech.note": "Scores are an expert fit rating (0–5), not a benchmark. Full rationale and risks — in <code>docs/adr-0001-engine.md</code>.",

    "arch.title": "System architecture",
    "arch.lead": "How the project is built: system layers, the data model and the life cycle of a single network frame. Switch tabs.",
    "arch.tab1": "🧱 System layers",
    "arch.tab2": "🖱️ Layers — interactive",
    "arch.tab3": "🗄️ Data ER diagram",
    "arch.tab4": "🗂️ ER schema — interactive",
    "arch.tab5": "🔁 Frame sequence",
    "arch.layersNote": "Arrows show data flow; the solid line between client and server is the binary network protocol. To explore by layer, open the interactive tab.",
    "arch.interNote": "Hover a layer to highlight it, and click to expand its components and description.",
    "arch.erNote": "Tables are grouped by meaning: identity, world, content, economy. Relations are 1&nbsp;→&nbsp;N by foreign keys (FK).",
    "arch.erdNote": "Click any table — only its relations are highlighted. Clicking a table in the list also opens its card and highlights relations.",
    "arch.seqNote": "Full cycle: input → client prediction → authoritative server → state delta → reconciliation and interpolation.",
    "arch.c1t": "Frame flow",
    "arch.c1p": "Input → client prediction → delta sent → authoritative server tick → reconciliation and interpolation on the client. This is what keeps the world fair.",
    "arch.c2t": "Separation of concerns",
    "arch.c2p": "The client handles rendering and responsiveness; the server owns the truth: movement, voxel, inventory, economy and validation.",
    "arch.c3t": "Scaling",
    "arch.c3p": "The world is split by star systems and zones; a spatial index and interest management keep thousands of players online under control.",
    "arch.c4t": "Persistence",
    "arch.c4p": "Transactional data in PostgreSQL, heavy voxel chunks and blueprints in object storage. Everything players build is saved.",
    "arch.c5t": "Trust",
    "arch.c5p": "Player scripting runs sandboxed with limits, and the server re-validates every action — the basis of anti-cheat.",
    "arch.c6t": "Infrastructure",
    "arch.c6p": "Kubernetes, autoscaling by region, monitoring and backups. The world runs 24/7 without downtime.",

    "code.title": "Code: server core",
    "code.lead": "The single-shard core is already written in Rust and works: deterministic simulation, binary protocol, tick loop and interest management. It builds and is covered by tests.",
    "code.c1t": "Determinism",
    "code.c1p": "Custom trigonometry, custom PRNG and a fixed 30 Hz step: server and client compute the world bit-for-bit identically. Verified by checksum.",
    "code.c2t": "World generation",
    "code.c2p": "Star systems, planets, moons and asteroid belts are generated from a seed — reproducible. Black holes are rare.",
    "code.c3t": "UDP and deltas",
    "code.c3p": "Real UDP transport with a session token and batching. Only changed entities in view travel over the network.",
    "code.c4t": "Spatial index",
    "code.c4p": "A uniform grid: interest management visits only nearby cells, not the whole world. Verified against brute force.",
    "code.c5t": "Interest management",
    "code.c5p": "A client sees only what is nearby. Radius is 2000 units, index cell size is 1000 units.",
    "code.c6t": "Netcode",
    "code.c6p": "Client prediction and reconciliation: divergence from the server is fixed by replaying unacknowledged frames.",

    "engine.title": "Engine: rendering the world",
    "engine.lead": "Per ADR-0001 the client is Unreal Engine 5: the engine is installed, the module is built and the editor opens a real 3D scene. While the UE client grows its gameplay, the world can also be seen through a <b>custom Rust renderer</b> — a true CPU ray tracer. It draws <b>the same world</b> that arrives over the network, and that is provable — the frames below are generated by code from the repository.",
    "engine.c1t": "Ray tracing",
    "engine.c1p": "Ray intersections with spheres (planets, stars) and oriented blocks (ships, asteroids). 2×2 supersampling per pixel.",
    "engine.c2t": "Procedural worlds",
    "engine.c2p": "Planet terrain and nebulae are fractal noise (value noise with interpolation). Fully deterministic, no external libraries.",
    "engine.c3t": "Block constructions",
    "engine.c3p": "Ships and asteroids are made of blocks — the same voxel aesthetic as in-game building.",

    "plan.title": "Development plan",
    "plan.lead": "The full plan from concept to live-ops. Click a phase to expand its tasks. Statuses update live from <code>data.js</code>/<code>plan.json</code>.",
    "progress.title": "Progress",
    "progress.lead": "Overall completion is computed automatically across all plan tasks.",
    "roadmap.title": "Roadmap",
    "roadmap.lead": "A short timeline of the phases. The heading with status updates as work progresses.",

